# Game-derived material - NEVER commit, and never keep in this tree.
# The game EXE, any analysis project built from it, and decompiler output are
# copyrighted works of Red Barrels and have no place here. What this repository
# holds is our own findings about the interface: RVAs, struct offsets and notes.
OLGame.exe
*.gpr
*.rep/
*.gzf
*.idb
*.i64
*_decomp.c
*_decompiled.c

# Scratch working directory for a local investigation session, and the bulky,
# non-deliverable output such a session produces: screenshots and frame grabs,
# memory dumps, traces and captured logs. None of it belongs in a public repo -
# and deleting the branch later does not unpublish it, because the host keeps
# serving every blob by SHA until it garbage-collects. Ignore the directory and
# keep the files on disk.
.re/
*.dmp
*.log
*.trace
*.bin
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.bmp
# The README demo clip is the one carve-out (see AGENTS.md), so assets/ is kept.
!assets/**
